# Maintainer: AstroOS <https://github.com/bakathefish/ASTRO-OS>
# Contributor: Antonio Rojas <arojas@archlinux.org> (the Arch recipe this follows)
#
# plasma-welcome, rebuilt with one page changed. On a live medium the Welcome
# Center's first page (src/qml/pages/Live.qml) draws the distribution's logo a
# second time behind the "Install" button: a copy sixteen grid units wide,
# blurred, at ten percent opacity, meant as a glow. With a logo that already
# carries its own glow and a bright ring the copy reads as a second planet
# with a faint wordmark through it (2026-09-06 screenshot: "two AstroOS logos
# on top of each other"). The QML is compiled into the binary, so no file on
# disk can override it; the patch removes the blurred copy and the
# QtQuick.Effects import that only served it.
#
# Two more patches, same day, same screenshots:
# 0002: the "Install" button on that page (src/public/qml/ApplicationIcon.qml)
#   is a ToolButton with a custom content item. The org.kde.desktop style
#   paints a ToolButton's own icon and text through QStyle in its background,
#   underneath any content item, so a small "[icon] Install AstroOS" label
#   showed through the large icon as a second, offset planet. The button now
#   carries no icon or text of its own; the content item draws both.
# 0003: Calamares runs as root through pkexec and talks to the session bus,
#   which starts a root session bus, which activates a root kded6, which loads
#   this module, which (LiveEnvironment=true in the system plasma-welcomerc)
#   opened a second Welcome Center over the user's session halfway through the
#   installation (journal: dbus-daemon "[session uid=0]" then
#   plasma-welcome "Failed to register with host portal"). The kded module
#   now does nothing when it runs as root. Nothing else changes.
#
# provides/conflicts/replaces plasma-welcome: plasma-meta depends on
# plasma-welcome by name, and libalpm resolves a dependency from the target
# set before it looks at the repositories, so listing this package explicitly
# (astroos/meta/astroos-core.list) is what makes it the one installed, on the
# ISO and by the installer alike. Same version as the Plasma release the rest
# of the desktop comes from; rebuild when Plasma moves.
#
# Source and signature are KDE's own release files, verified against the
# release manager's key vendored under keys/pgp/ (the lane imports it before
# makepkg; see build-aur-repo.sh). 6.7.4 is signed by Bhushan Shah's signing
# subkey B3CB366552540BE06EE9AD9711968C44928CAEFC; the primary key fingerprint
# below is the one Arch's recipe names for him. The tarball's sha256 was
# checked against Arch's recipe and against a download of our own
# (2026-09-06) and both agree.
pkgname=astroos-plasma-welcome
pkgver=6.7.4
pkgrel=1
pkgdesc="AstroOS onboarding wizard for Plasma: plasma-welcome, with the live page drawing the logo once"
arch=(x86_64)
url="https://kde.org/plasma-desktop/"
license=(LGPL-2.0-or-later)
depends=(glibc
         kcmutils
         kconfig
         kcoreaddons
         kcrash
         kdbusaddons
         kglobalaccel
         ki18n
         kio
         kirigami
         kirigami-addons
         kjobwidgets
         knewstuff
         kservice
         ksvg
         kuserfeedback
         kwindowsystem
         libplasma
         libstdc++
         plasma-nm
         plasma5support
         qt6-5compat
         qt6-base
         qt6-declarative)
makedepends=(extra-cmake-modules)
provides=("plasma-welcome=$pkgver")
conflicts=(plasma-welcome)
replaces=(plasma-welcome)
_dirver=$(echo $pkgver | cut -d. -f1-3)
source=("https://download.kde.org/stable/plasma/$_dirver/plasma-welcome-$pkgver.tar.xz"{,.sig}
        0001-live-page-no-blurred-second-logo.patch
        0002-application-icon-no-style-label.patch
        0003-kded-no-launch-as-root.patch)
sha256sums=('d9862440a16820ca00abb22363be57e9b156adc76db692d4d04cabd3e862ab3d'
            'SKIP'
